          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "line1": "<span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">About 20 percent of people affected by acute low back pain develop chronic low back pain with persistent symptoms at one year.<sup>1</sup>&nbsp;Rose was one of them. After trying to manage her low back pain for three years with conservative treatments, watch how Dr. Nima Salari restored her alignment and got Rose hiking again.</span>",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Feb 01 2022 16:23:17 GMT+0000",
